// Calyx of Held: the presynaptic giant terminal of the contralateral GBC axon,
// apposed to the MNTB principal-cell soma, and the source of the prespike.
//
// This is a separate presynaptic cell from the MNTB principal neuron. In the
// LFP pipeline it is a co-located auxiliary population driven by the same
// contralateral GBC spike train; its transmembrane current, a giant
// presynaptic AP, is the extracellular prespike that in vivo precedes the MNTB
// spike by ~0.5 ms and shapes ABR wave III. Its dipole sums with the principal
// cell's by linear superposition, at the same probe and head position.
//
// Geometry (Karadas 2021 [4]; Kulesza / Sierksma [7]):
//   The calyx engulfs more than half the MNTB soma. Karadas idealise it as a
//   half-ring (ring dia 13 um, wall 2 um), but that thin arc (~126 um2)
//   understates the apposed area and so both the prespike and the cleft
//   potential. It is modelled here as the engulfing cup: a cylinder dia 8 um,
//   length 20 um along z (area ~500 um2, about half the 1257 um2 soma).
//   precalyx_axon is the final unmyelinated pre-terminal segment, with high Na,
//   and is the primary presynaptic current sink (Karadas: the pre-calyx axon
//   Na at ~0.2 nS/um2 = 0.02 S/cm2 generates the prespike sink). It runs along
//   +x (mediolateral), the GBC axon's approach across the midline.
//
// Channel densities at the terminal face (Karadas [4], converted pS/um2 to
//   S/cm2, where 1 nS/um2 = 0.1 S/cm2):
//     Na  200 pS/um2 -> 0.020 S/cm2   (Ca 40 pS/um2 omitted: no Ca mod in
//     KLT 240 pS/um2 -> 0.024 S/cm2    models/mso, and Na dominates the field)
//     KHT  80 pS/um2 -> 0.008 S/cm2
//   The precalyx_axon uses a higher nodal Na so it reliably spikes and drives
//   the terminal. Fast Na is namntb (models/mntb/namntb.mod); klt and kht
//   kinetics come from models/mso.
//
// The cleft leak conductance g_cl ~ 1.0 uS (R_cleft ~ 1 MOhm; Sierksma 2021
// [7]) is applied in the LFP and validation drivers through NEURON's
// extracellular mechanism (xg set so xg*area = g_cl), giving a cleft node
// whose potential rises several mV during the presynaptic AP.

create precalyx_axon, calyx

access precalyx_axon

// Pre-terminal axon (+x -> origin), high Na = primary presynaptic sink
precalyx_axon {
    nseg = 5
    Ra   = 150
    cm   = 1.0
    insert pas
    g_pas = 1.0e-3
    e_pas = -70.0
    insert namntb
    gbar_namntb = 0.30
    ena = 55.0
    insert kht
    gbar_kht = 0.015
    insert klt
    gbar_klt = 0.010
    ek = -77.0
    pt3dadd(30, 0, 0, 1.5)
    pt3dadd( 5, 0, 0, 1.5)
}

// Calyx terminal (half-ring, arc ~20 um along z, tube dia 2 um), apposed to soma
calyx {
    nseg = 5
    Ra   = 150
    cm   = 1.0
    insert pas
    g_pas = 1.0e-3
    e_pas = -70.0
    insert namntb
    gbar_namntb = 0.020
    ena = 55.0
    insert klt
    gbar_klt = 0.024
    insert kht
    gbar_kht = 0.008
    ek = -77.0
    pt3dadd(0, 0, -10, 8)
    pt3dadd(0, 0,  10, 8)
}

connect calyx(0), precalyx_axon(1)
